This report presents the initial observation of the $B^0_s\to\bar{D}^0 K^0_L$ decay mode and provides evidence for the $B^0_s\to\bar{D}^{*0} K^0_L process. The analysis is based on $3.0\,\text{fb}^{-1}$ of integrated luminosity from $pp$ collisions at $\sqrt{s}=7\,\text{TeV}$ collected by the LHCb experiment. The measured branching fractions are given as
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{B}(B^0_s\to\bar{D}^0 K^0_L) &=(4.49\pm0.43\pm0.21)\times 10^{-4}, \\
\mathcal{B}(B^0_s\to\bar{D}^{*0} K^0_L) &=(7.17\pm0.50\pm0.21)\times 10^{-4}.
\end{align*}
Here, the first uncertainty represents statistical error while the second accounts for systematic uncertainties.
